  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Three shots in a row",
  "description": "Place three balls in a row just outside the penalty area, a couple of metres apart. The coach shoots ball one, the goalkeeper saves, the coach shoots ball two as soon as the goalkeeper is set again, and then ball three. The shots come close together, but the goalkeeper should have time to get set between them.\n\nPut the balls back and do another set, 4–6 sets with rest in between. Vary the order, for example the middle one first or right to left.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "After the save: straight back into your basic stance, eyes on the next ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Move sideways so you are square to the new ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Clear the rebound to the side or catch the ball – no rebound in front of the goal."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
